Since Bala Hatun became the leader of the
hatuns they have never missed a target!

197
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:54,800
Bala Hatun was raised by Sheik Edebalı.

198
00:18:55,600 --> 00:18:59,180
And with Aygül Hatun...

199
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:19,780
From now on is on Aygül and sisters.

200
00:19:20,140 --> 00:19:22,460
Conquest is deserved by who work.

201
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:24,460
I hope you all can experience it.

202
00:19:25,480 --> 00:19:26,960
I hope so.

203
00:19:27,540 --> 00:19:30,080
I will convey your trust to the alps.

204
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:36,160
Holofira will set off tomorrow.

205
00:19:36,820 --> 00:19:40,420
You've protected me. I am grateful to you.

206
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:51,480
What is it?

207
00:20:27,080 --> 00:20:28,780
It was my mother's necklace.

208
00:20:30,380 --> 00:20:31,860
It is beautiful.

209
00:21:00,360 --> 00:21:01,640
My Fatma!

210
00:21:03,080 --> 00:21:05,280
Oh, my beautiful daughter!

211
00:21:11,600 --> 00:21:13,260
My beautiful daughter!

212
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:21,380
My Fatma, what are you doing here?

213
00:21:21,450 --> 00:21:22,390
Are you all right?

214
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:32,400
He neither ate nor drank. We had to
bring her, Malhun Hatun.

215
00:21:37,900 --> 00:21:39,440
My beautiful daughter!

216
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:45,420
Welcome, my beautiful girl.

217
00:22:16,480 --> 00:22:20,660
A painful death will meet you when
you eat these.

218
00:22:21,560 --> 00:22:23,640
You will be held by the dark.

219
00:22:30,700 --> 00:22:32,420
People are coming!

220
00:22:48,060 --> 00:22:52,780
Since my daughter is beside me now,
I am relieved.

221
00:22:53,740 --> 00:22:54,780
I know, my sister.

222
00:22:55,540 --> 00:22:57,400
Missing a child is something else.

223
00:22:57,400 --> 00:22:59,060
Thankfully you met your child.

224
00:23:00,660 --> 00:23:03,540
I will be as happy as you when Osman Bey
and Barkın returns.

225
00:23:04,080 --> 00:23:05,720
They will, of course.

226
00:23:06,020 --> 00:23:08,120
Don't worry, sister.

227
00:23:08,500 --> 00:23:10,120
I hope so, Sister.

228
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:16,100
You did a great job in this short time,
Alaca.

229
00:23:17,480 --> 00:23:20,500
Come on, alps!
Load these to the carriages.

230
00:23:21,100 --> 00:23:24,040
We will set off in the morning tomorrow.

231
00:23:24,320 --> 00:23:25,460
Come on.

232
00:23:43,360 --> 00:23:45,820
I told you there will be no winner in
a war!

233
00:23:46,320 --> 00:23:48,120
Here we are, losing.

234
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:53,380
They lose because they kill and we lose
because we die.

235
00:23:54,300 --> 00:23:56,620
Starting this war was a huge mistake.

236
00:23:57,120 --> 00:24:00,580
Unfortunately, Lord Nikola was the one
to make this mistake.

237
00:24:01,460 --> 00:24:03,100
He started this war.

238
00:24:03,260 --> 00:24:06,400
And he sent us to the fire even
if he didn't want to.

239
00:24:06,900 --> 00:24:08,980
Lord Nikola is fighting for us.

240
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:12,140
-Are you defending the Turks?
-What are you saying?

241
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:15,100
Of course I don't!

242
00:24:15,300 --> 00:24:19,780
But, brothers, Lord Nikola worked for this
war to happen.

243
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:22,920
Look where we are now!

244
00:24:24,540 --> 00:24:27,340
If you don't have the power to fight
the enemy...

245
00:24:27,520 --> 00:24:31,300
...we must open our arms for hugs,
not for fists!

246
00:24:31,560 --> 00:24:35,260
I know that if we approach the Turks with
good intentions...

247
00:24:35,440 --> 00:24:37,260
...they will approach us the same way.

248
00:24:37,340 --> 00:24:39,260
Their intention is not to destroy us.

249
00:24:40,740 --> 00:24:43,200
If Lord Nikola started this war...

250
00:24:43,560 --> 00:24:45,600
...he should bear the consequences alone.

251
00:24:46,040 --> 00:24:49,020
We won't fight. We will be friends.

252
00:24:49,240 --> 00:24:53,700
Entering a war that we will lose will only
increase our pain.

253
00:24:53,840 --> 00:24:56,060
Osman wants to take the castle.

254
00:24:56,060 --> 00:24:58,800
Do you think he will let us live if he
takes the castle?

255
00:24:58,800 --> 00:25:00,800
-No! Not happening!
-No way!

256
00:25:00,800 --> 00:25:04,600
-No way! We will fight!
-They will kill us!

257
00:25:05,240 --> 00:25:06,460
Get off!

258
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:13,520
If Osman takes the castle...

259
00:25:14,260 --> 00:25:18,120
...you will be next to die after Nikola.

260
00:25:18,360 --> 00:25:19,680
I don't think so.

261
00:25:20,080 --> 00:25:24,200
The Turks will never do anything to a man
of religion that has no harm.

262
00:25:24,480 --> 00:25:26,940
I know them much better than you.

263
00:25:29,440 --> 00:25:32,920
Is this why you speak against Lord Nikola?

264
00:25:33,820 --> 00:25:37,260
Our soldiers have been watching you for
a while.

265
00:25:38,460 --> 00:25:41,520
Your tongue will cause you big trouble,
Priest.

266
00:25:42,520 --> 00:25:45,660
We are taking you to the dungeon by
the order of Lord Nikola.

267
00:25:45,760 --> 00:25:48,750
-No, we won't let you take him!
-He has done nothing! No way!

268
00:25:48,750 --> 00:25:51,000
-You can't take him!
-We won't let you take him!

269
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:53,000
Enough!

270
00:25:57,820 --> 00:25:59,920
Our dungeons are big enough!

271
00:26:03,360 --> 00:26:06,120
Does anyone want to rebel?

272
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:10,760
Good.

273
00:26:11,840 --> 00:26:13,020
Tie him.

274
00:26:24,700 --> 00:26:26,800
Allah is one!

275
00:26:30,920 --> 00:26:33,860
Allah hears those who praise Him!

276
00:26:34,960 --> 00:26:37,620
Allah is one!

277
00:26:39,980 --> 00:26:42,260
Allah is one!

278
00:26:44,820 --> 00:26:47,020
Allah is one!

279
00:26:50,380 --> 00:26:53,780
Allah is one!

280
00:27:13,760 --> 00:27:16,800
May Allah's peace, mercy and blessings
be upon you.

281
00:27:17,320 --> 00:27:20,780
May Allah's peace, mercy and blessings
be upon you.

282
00:27:30,380 --> 00:27:35,120
Oh our Mighty and Forever Allah!

283
00:27:35,360 --> 00:27:41,320
This army only kneels to you.

284
00:27:42,740 --> 00:27:46,500
They fear neither death nor injury.

285
00:27:47,640 --> 00:27:53,330
Our Prophet calls this army veteran.

286
00:27:54,420 --> 00:27:56,880
They are heroes from the heart.

287
00:27:57,160 --> 00:27:59,440
They are all Turkish warriors.

288
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:02,740
O, Mightiest of All!

289
00:28:03,100 --> 00:28:09,280
May you grant your prophet Muhammad
Mustafa a comrade...

290
00:28:12,020 --> 00:28:13,300
...to this army.

291
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:14,840
Amen!

292
00:28:15,400 --> 00:28:21,140
Grant so that the infidels can't defeat
the warriors of the Right!

293
00:28:21,140 --> 00:28:23,960
-Amen!
-Amen!

294
00:28:24,500 --> 00:28:26,540
Grant us Muhammad Mustafa...

295
00:28:29,700 --> 00:28:31,340
...as their comrade so that...

296
00:28:32,020 --> 00:28:36,460
...your great name can be heard all over
the world.

297
00:28:36,460 --> 00:28:39,100
-Amen!
-Amen!

298
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:42,060
O, the Victorious!

299
00:28:42,760 --> 00:28:44,900
O, the Victorious!

300
00:28:45,660 --> 00:28:47,460
O, the Victorious!

301
00:28:48,520 --> 00:28:51,580
May you grant our army the victory.

302
00:28:51,580 --> 00:28:54,340
-Amen!
-Amen!

303
00:28:54,380 --> 00:28:57,900
May you make their victory permanent!

304
00:28:57,900 --> 00:29:00,040
-Amen!
-Amen!

305
00:29:02,040 --> 00:29:05,120
Amen! Surah El-Fatiha!

306
00:29:28,740 --> 00:29:31,000
Inegöl Castle

307
00:29:42,820 --> 00:29:46,080
So, Lord Nikola is the one to blame.
Is that so?

308
00:29:52,220 --> 00:29:55,580
No one can harm this city as much as
Nikola.

309
00:29:57,040 --> 00:30:00,600
If you don't attack Turks, they will
approach you friendly.

310
00:30:02,140 --> 00:30:04,880
But Nikola is a savage.

311
00:30:06,240 --> 00:30:08,200
None of us matter to him.

312
00:30:08,300 --> 00:30:09,780
Neither are you.

313
00:30:10,180 --> 00:30:13,200
You'll regret what you said, Pristo.

314
00:30:29,200 --> 00:30:30,540
Will I regret what I said?

315
00:30:32,040 --> 00:30:33,300
Is he going to kill me?

316
00:30:34,260 --> 00:30:35,740
Is he going to torture me?

317
00:30:37,240 --> 00:30:39,100
What else can he do to me?

318
00:30:48,300 --> 00:30:50,840
I'll take care of this
disrespectful priest.

319
00:31:00,160 --> 00:31:02,100
Your poisonous tongue...

320
00:31:03,340 --> 00:31:06,580
...makes Lord Nikola
very angry, Priest Prisso.

321
00:31:08,580 --> 00:31:10,940
I'm afraid that will lead to your demise.

322
00:31:12,100 --> 00:31:13,780
I am not afraid of Nikola.

323
00:31:15,200 --> 00:31:18,820
He already killed the entire
city by starting this war.

324
00:31:20,200 --> 00:31:22,280
Instead of seeing Nikola in İnegöl...

325
00:31:23,360 --> 00:31:26,140
...I would rather live under
the auspices of Osman Bey.

326
00:31:27,480 --> 00:31:30,620
I know of his and his father's mercy.

327
00:31:36,640 --> 00:31:40,220
It seems it'll take a while for
this priest to come to his senses.

328
00:31:41,780 --> 00:31:42,880
You guys leave.

329
00:31:44,060 --> 00:31:45,220
I said leave!

330
00:32:04,240 --> 00:32:07,240
If you want to stay
alive, stay quiet, priest.

331
00:32:07,720 --> 00:32:09,720
Or, you won't get out of here alive.

332
00:32:11,060 --> 00:32:13,260
Stay quiet and wait.

333
00:32:13,660 --> 00:32:15,260
Just wait.

334
00:32:17,580 --> 00:32:18,960
How could this happen?

335
00:32:19,440 --> 00:32:21,520
You're better off not knowing anything.

336
00:32:22,580 --> 00:32:24,400
Therefore, don't ask
any questions either.

337
00:32:44,260 --> 00:32:46,490
Osman is hitting us
with everything he has.

338
00:32:50,780 --> 00:32:54,880
Even I can't save you
after this mess, Nikola.

339
00:32:57,960 --> 00:33:01,480
My soldiers are waiting for my
command outside and I'm stuck here.

340
00:33:04,000 --> 00:33:06,760
Do you see those soldiers, Romanos?

341
00:33:07,960 --> 00:33:10,900
They're all good at what they do.

342
00:33:11,060 --> 00:33:13,980
They're going to protect
our walls, don't worry.

343
00:33:14,100 --> 00:33:16,260
Osman and those shepherd alps...

344
00:33:16,500 --> 00:33:19,400
...will be sorry they were born.

345
00:33:19,600 --> 00:33:23,360
Be real Nikola, be real.

346
00:33:24,420 --> 00:33:26,220
This is not a Khan battle.

347
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:28,660
The weapons, equipments...

348
00:33:28,800 --> 00:33:32,280
...and an army is waiting
to kill you outside.

349
00:33:36,600 --> 00:33:38,900
Your soldiers are strong,
I'll give you that...

350
00:33:38,940 --> 00:33:40,780
...but don't underestimate Osman.

351
00:33:41,820 --> 00:33:43,840
If this siege keeps on longer...

352
00:33:44,520 --> 00:33:46,720
...he'll get the upper hand.

353
00:33:47,030 --> 00:33:49,900
Do you think I haven't thought
those things through, Romanos?

354
00:33:49,900 --> 00:33:53,330
For years, I've been thinking
of this, day in and day out!

355
00:33:53,800 --> 00:33:57,280
Do you know what is one of the major
things that make a siege a failure?

356
00:33:57,920 --> 00:34:02,820
Famine. If your are left hungry...

357
00:34:03,130 --> 00:34:06,140
...you'll never and I mean never succeed.

358
00:34:06,700 --> 00:34:10,969
That's why our warehouses
are full of food.

359
00:34:11,750 --> 00:34:12,760
But,...

360
00:34:13,179 --> 00:34:17,330
But if a disease starts spreading
amongst the people...

361
00:34:18,739 --> 00:34:20,590
...you won't have anything else to do.

362
00:34:20,679 --> 00:34:22,480
Exactly, Romanos.

363
00:34:22,710 --> 00:34:26,149
That's why he have enough
ammuniton for Osman.

364
00:34:26,460 --> 00:34:29,300
But it is an epidemic disease.

365
00:34:30,159 --> 00:34:32,219
An epidemic disease.

366
00:34:32,639 --> 00:34:37,480
I Aya Nikola, Romanos, took preacutions.

367
00:34:38,050 --> 00:34:41,159
They won't know that hit them.

368
00:34:48,199 --> 00:34:51,460
Hell is coming for you.

369
00:34:56,520 --> 00:34:59,640
Allahu Akbar!

370
00:35:04,320 --> 00:35:08,740
We've been hitting them since daytime.

371
00:35:09,100 --> 00:35:11,830
The shots keep hitting them
without stopping, Osman Bey.

372
00:35:12,810 --> 00:35:14,350
Pull!

373
00:35:18,530 --> 00:35:20,450
Die!

374
00:35:22,980 --> 00:35:24,800
Allahu Akbar!

375
00:35:30,300 --> 00:35:32,670
We've been hitting them all day...

376
00:35:33,280 --> 00:35:36,800
...but could not breach once.

377
00:35:37,730 --> 00:35:43,470
We'll accomplish our goals with the
strength and the patience from Allah.

378
00:35:44,090 --> 00:35:47,670
Patience will get us what
we aim to achieve, Turgut Bey.

379
00:35:48,790 --> 00:35:52,500
We will breach the walls
of İnegöl, if Allah permits.

380
00:35:52,660 --> 00:35:54,210
If Allah permits.

381
00:35:55,050 --> 00:35:57,220
There is no turning back.

382
00:35:59,440 --> 00:36:02,670
İnegöl will belong to the Turks.

383
00:36:04,130 --> 00:36:06,140
Well said, Osman Bey!

384
00:36:07,150 --> 00:36:11,470
We will be patient but it would
be better if we could breach soon.

385
00:36:11,970 --> 00:36:14,130
What are we going to do if we fail?

386
00:36:14,580 --> 00:36:17,500
We're exposed here to the enemy.

387
00:36:18,180 --> 00:36:21,450
Barkın Bey is right, the
siege may take months.

388
00:36:21,930 --> 00:36:24,070
What if the emperor sends an army?

389
00:36:24,940 --> 00:36:28,910
İnegöl is full of food and water,
they can endure us for months.

390
00:36:29,330 --> 00:36:34,610
Even Mongolians can get the
word and come after us from here.

391
00:36:37,040 --> 00:36:39,930
One has to come to a conquest with faith.

392
00:36:41,850 --> 00:36:47,900
But it is not the time to
make you have faith.

393
00:36:49,460 --> 00:36:53,240
I don't tell anyone to stay or go.

394
00:36:54,190 --> 00:36:58,720
But if anyone has doubt...

395
00:37:00,050 --> 00:37:02,030
...they don't need to follow me.

396
00:37:02,630 --> 00:37:03,980
Never, Osman Bey.

397
00:37:04,800 --> 00:37:07,810
There is neither doubt nor fear among us.

398
00:37:08,350 --> 00:37:10,620
We will follow you.

399
00:37:11,160 --> 00:37:17,610
We came to the walls of İnegöl for
the establishment of a government.

400
00:37:18,850 --> 00:37:23,030
We came here to drink
the sherbet of martrydom.

401
00:37:25,850 --> 00:37:29,860
As we decided with Gündüz Bey...

402
00:37:30,770 --> 00:37:33,400
...we will get the catapults
in front of the walls.

403
00:37:33,760 --> 00:37:36,780
And Gündüz Bey will keep
hitting them, with patience.

404
00:37:37,840 --> 00:37:40,100
We will hit them with
the wrath of the Turks.

405
00:37:40,700 --> 00:37:43,650
With the belief of Allah.

406
00:37:45,190 --> 00:37:49,640
We will have the breaches
that will make İnegöl our land.

407
00:37:50,340 --> 00:37:52,180
Do not forget...

408
00:37:52,990 --> 00:37:56,980
...it is not the strength of the
arrow that cracks the shield...

409
00:37:58,250 --> 00:38:00,250
...it is the quantity of it.

410
00:38:02,190 --> 00:38:06,270
I'd like to lead the alps when
the breaches are open, my Bey.

411
00:38:06,810 --> 00:38:08,810
Whoever goes in first goes down quickly.

412
00:38:09,160 --> 00:38:14,050
Therefore, after going in, you should
counter the attack as you go in.

413
00:38:16,150 --> 00:38:17,280
My bey,...

414
00:38:18,440 --> 00:38:22,270
...if you allow it, I'd like
to go in with Konur.

415
00:38:22,590 --> 00:38:25,560
Of course, you may go in.

416
00:38:26,250 --> 00:38:27,970
May Allah bless you, my bey!

417
00:38:29,240 --> 00:38:34,430
We will be the first ones to plant
the bloody and glorious flag of İnegöl.

418
00:38:37,090 --> 00:38:41,740
İnegöl is at the paw of the
wolf, there is no turning back.

419
00:38:42,540 --> 00:38:48,470
We will be victorious for our government.

420
00:38:50,070 --> 00:38:52,810
Let's burn the infidels, brothers!

421
00:38:53,170 --> 00:38:56,220
Come on my lions, light it up!

422
00:38:58,930 --> 00:39:00,020
Load it up!

423
00:39:00,670 --> 00:39:04,280
Nikola!

424
00:39:06,440 --> 00:39:08,390
Allahu Akbar!

425
00:39:09,360 --> 00:39:12,730
Let's throw these fires at
the infidels, my brothers!

426
00:39:29,510 --> 00:39:31,990
Soldiers!

427
00:39:33,640 --> 00:39:37,180
Soldier! Soldiers!

428
00:39:38,180 --> 00:39:42,280
Soldiers of Byzantine!

429
00:39:42,570 --> 00:39:47,310
Sons of Byzantine, don't you dare dying
before bloodying up your swords!

430
00:39:47,430 --> 00:39:51,390
If your swords are
not riddled with blood...

431
00:39:51,490 --> 00:39:54,240
...I will kill you with my sword!

432
00:39:54,340 --> 00:39:57,820
Archers, get to your positions!

433
00:39:57,850 --> 00:39:59,440
Get to your positions!

434
00:39:59,530 --> 00:40:01,450
Don't fall down!

435
00:40:01,540 --> 00:40:05,590
Don't fall down, for
your castle, for Rome!

436
00:40:06,030 --> 00:40:10,240
For Rome! Come on!

437
00:40:11,900 --> 00:40:13,480
Let's go!

438
00:40:14,590 --> 00:40:16,170
Osman!

439
00:40:16,730 --> 00:40:19,130
We don't blindly get stubborn.

440
00:40:19,650 --> 00:40:22,380
We do what we say we want to do.

441
00:40:23,320 --> 00:40:29,090
If the siege draws out, we'll
be prepared accordingly.

442
00:40:29,540 --> 00:40:32,380
How, Osman Bey?

443
00:40:34,280 --> 00:40:39,350
We will make sure no one
comes for the aid of İnegöl.

444
00:40:42,040 --> 00:40:43,480
Rahman Bey,...

445
00:40:44,010 --> 00:40:49,090
...in order to stop the
aid coming from İznik...

446
00:40:49,510 --> 00:40:52,850
...you'll be positioned at
Köprühisar with your alps.

447
00:40:53,230 --> 00:40:56,980
May Allah bless you, Osman Bey!
Whoever helps the cruel deserves to die.

448
00:40:57,670 --> 00:40:59,060
May Allah bless you!

449
00:41:00,820 --> 00:41:05,370
Durmuş Bey, you take a position
in Akhisar with your valiants.

450
00:41:05,660 --> 00:41:07,520
Until İnegöl belongs to Islam...

451
00:41:07,650 --> 00:41:10,270
...we won't let anyone
get near it, Osman Bey.

452
00:41:10,490 --> 00:41:11,840
May Allah bless you!

453
00:41:12,510 --> 00:41:13,560
Barkın Bey,...

454
00:41:14,270 --> 00:41:18,960
...you get one of your best alps
and divide into two groups.

455
00:41:19,340 --> 00:41:22,820
You and your alps get
positioned in Adranus.

456
00:41:23,240 --> 00:41:26,150
The rest will get in
position in Koyunhisar.

457
00:41:26,270 --> 00:41:27,820
May Allah bless you, Osman Bey!

458
00:41:30,010 --> 00:41:33,400
Come on, get on the road before sunset.

459
00:41:34,270 --> 00:41:39,160
May Allah protect you!

460
00:41:39,400 --> 00:41:41,130
May Allah bless you!

461
00:41:48,270 --> 00:41:50,340
Allahu Akbar!

462
00:42:07,130 --> 00:42:09,070
May I come in, my bey?

463
00:42:11,350 --> 00:42:14,180
Come in, Hüsamettin, come.

464
00:42:20,910 --> 00:42:24,310
You will send word to Nikola immediately.

465
00:42:25,570 --> 00:42:27,440
The castle is under siege, my bey.

466
00:42:28,550 --> 00:42:33,650
Do we need to go to the castle
to send word, Hüsamettin?

467
00:42:35,580 --> 00:42:38,760
You will walk about twenty
steps from the left of Kızılağaç.

468
00:42:39,270 --> 00:42:42,770
When you get to the right location,
look at the edge of the castle.

469
00:42:44,040 --> 00:42:49,600
You will throw this arrow
to where the two flags stand.

470
00:42:54,900 --> 00:42:57,440
A soldier is waiting for you there.

471
00:42:59,620 --> 00:43:03,090
- Come on, go.
- Yes, my bey!

472
00:43:10,250 --> 00:43:12,690
My men are waiting here.

473
00:43:13,940 --> 00:43:17,190
We will surround there headquarters
as soon as the explosions start.

474
00:43:17,390 --> 00:43:21,090
They will be crushed.

475
00:43:21,690 --> 00:43:27,230
Their headquarters will be destroyed.

476
00:43:35,560 --> 00:43:39,610
Sir, a word from one of
the spies amongst them.

477
00:43:59,880 --> 00:44:03,213
Looks like your birds sent
you some good news, Nikola.

478
00:44:03,460 --> 00:44:06,310
Very good news, Romanos.

479
00:44:06,580 --> 00:44:10,000
Osman scattered the ones
that came from different tents.

480
00:44:10,000 --> 00:44:12,260
So that they could protect
the important areas.

481
00:44:12,260 --> 00:44:16,420
On top of that, he said some
of his own men with them.

482
00:44:16,510 --> 00:44:23,290
I mean, Osman's army
is unguarded, Romanos.

483
00:44:28,710 --> 00:44:30,070
Good.

484
00:44:31,370 --> 00:44:34,130
I'll get on the move
immediately to lead my men.

485
00:44:36,130 --> 00:44:39,180
As soon as I unite with them,
I'll attack their post.

486
00:44:39,980 --> 00:44:44,940
When their post collapses, I
will burn all of their catapults.

487
00:44:46,900 --> 00:44:51,510
Osman won't be amount to
anything without his catapults.

488
00:44:51,880 --> 00:44:57,400
Also, he won't have a post
to position his army at.

489
00:44:57,620 --> 00:45:00,580
He will be in trouble.

490
00:45:00,700 --> 00:45:05,250
As you are assaulting Osman's post, I will
send all my soldiers to where Osman is.

491
00:45:08,850 --> 00:45:10,020
The only difficulty...

492
00:45:12,090 --> 00:45:15,680
...will be me going to Karasu
through the secret creek bed...

493
00:45:17,610 --> 00:45:21,250
...when Osman and his men
are this near to the walls.

494
00:45:21,990 --> 00:45:24,440
Take some brave men with you.

495
00:45:25,350 --> 00:45:26,800
Get on the road.

496
00:45:31,320 --> 00:45:36,120
Give just three brave men...

497
00:45:37,370 --> 00:45:40,730
...so that I can destroy an
army of three thousand for you.

498
00:45:44,960 --> 00:45:48,500
But make sure you're guys are ruthless.

499
00:45:48,680 --> 00:45:50,190
Captain Romanos,...

500
00:45:52,570 --> 00:45:55,740
...sir, they attacked
our honor in Bilecik.

501
00:45:56,140 --> 00:45:58,880
Now, you're going to kill them.

502
00:45:59,100 --> 00:46:01,120
Let me come with you.

503
00:46:03,810 --> 00:46:07,330
Both dying and killing along
side you is an honour, sir!

504
00:46:39,070 --> 00:46:41,370
May peace and mercy
of Allah be upon you!

505
00:46:43,310 --> 00:46:45,530
May peace and mercy
of Allah be upon you!

506
00:46:53,760 --> 00:46:57,590
Creator of all the almighty Allah,...

507
00:46:59,360 --> 00:47:01,860
...master of all, the almighty Allah,...

508
00:47:02,730 --> 00:47:05,370
...I pray to you to protect
me from the enemy...

509
00:47:07,630 --> 00:47:11,890
...you are the mightiest.

510
00:47:13,560 --> 00:47:15,030
My Allah,...

511
00:47:16,080 --> 00:47:22,240
...I pray to you for the
protection of my son Aktemur,...

512
00:47:22,750 --> 00:47:29,730
...my brother Osman, my innocent
nephews, and all Turmens...

513
00:47:31,400 --> 00:47:32,960
...dear Allah.

514
00:47:33,830 --> 00:47:38,110
Protect them from the devil and
from our enemies, dear Allah!

515
00:47:40,290 --> 00:47:41,640
My Allah,...

516
00:47:42,890 --> 00:47:47,990
...protect my son Aktemur...

517
00:47:48,620 --> 00:47:51,140
...have him be your follower.

518
00:47:53,820 --> 00:47:55,280
Make him a son befitting...

519
00:47:57,220 --> 00:48:02,110
...Islam and his forefathers,
make him an alp!

520
00:48:06,700 --> 00:48:09,050
They say the prayer of
the father for his son...

521
00:48:11,250 --> 00:48:14,510
...is similar to the prayer of
prophet Muhammed's for ummah.

522
00:48:18,990 --> 00:48:21,370
I am content with my child, dear Allah.

523
00:48:23,160 --> 00:48:25,960
May he be a worthy servant to you.

524
00:48:28,610 --> 00:48:30,220
Amen!

525
00:48:37,330 --> 00:48:40,240
May I come in, Gündüz Bey?

526
00:48:41,340 --> 00:48:43,050
Come in, Cerkutay.

527
00:48:49,330 --> 00:48:52,650
- May Allah accept your prayer, my bey!
- May Allah bless you!

528
00:48:54,220 --> 00:48:57,930
I sent the picket alps
as you wished, my bey.

529
00:48:59,080 --> 00:49:00,800
Thank you, Cerkutay!

530
00:49:02,360 --> 00:49:03,980
Thank you!

531
00:49:08,240 --> 00:49:10,990
Your mind is at Aktemur, right, my bey?

532
00:49:19,370 --> 00:49:20,920
Yes.

533
00:49:22,500 --> 00:49:24,930
Having a child is sometihng else.

534
00:49:27,820 --> 00:49:33,370
Ever since I've had kids, even
my sleeps are different, my bey.

535
00:49:34,890 --> 00:49:39,100
My mind and my heart are always with them.

536
00:49:42,120 --> 00:49:44,420
May Allah protect our children!

537
00:49:46,030 --> 00:49:47,590
Amen!

538
00:49:48,640 --> 00:49:52,340
Let's reunite with them safely as
soon as possible, if Allah permits.

539
00:49:53,000 --> 00:49:54,200
If Allah permits.

540
00:49:57,200 --> 00:49:58,920
If Allah permits, Cerkutay.

541
00:50:00,470 --> 00:50:02,340
Inshallah(if Allah permits), my valiant.

542
00:50:02,620 --> 00:50:04,300
Once we conquer İnegöl...

543
00:50:05,220 --> 00:50:09,600
I'll unite with my Aktemur and
you'll unite with your children.

544
00:50:11,200 --> 00:50:12,250
Don't worry.

545
00:50:12,600 --> 00:50:13,900
Amin.

546
00:50:14,770 --> 00:50:16,170
I don't worry, my bey.

547
00:50:17,120 --> 00:50:20,430
Saltuk takes care of his siblings.

548
00:50:34,500 --> 00:50:35,650
Should we go?

549
00:50:38,150 --> 00:50:39,600
We should, Cerkutay.

550
00:50:48,310 --> 00:50:50,670
İnegöl Castle

551
00:50:50,700 --> 00:50:53,590
In front of the Northern Walls

552
00:50:55,320 --> 00:50:58,700
With All Mighty Allah's
approval...

553
00:50:59,370 --> 00:51:00,570
raise it!

554
00:51:05,650 --> 00:51:06,950
Release it!

555
00:51:40,600 --> 00:51:41,900
Release!

556
00:52:00,520 --> 00:52:01,650
Brother.

557
00:52:03,470 --> 00:52:05,770
Tell me what's bothering you.

558
00:52:07,920 --> 00:52:12,820
I have nothing but the haste
of conquest, Osman Bey.

559
00:52:13,070 --> 00:52:16,020
My only prayer is for this
hole to be opened.

560
00:52:18,420 --> 00:52:22,300
Brother, whatever bothers you...

561
00:52:23,050 --> 00:52:24,900
can be seen through your face.

562
00:52:27,150 --> 00:52:29,870
Tell me.
Tell me, brother.

563
00:52:30,870 --> 00:52:33,500
It's obvious that you are hiding it.

564
00:52:40,320 --> 00:52:41,720
My child.

565
00:52:42,270 --> 00:52:43,870
Aktemur.

566
00:52:45,300 --> 00:52:49,120
What is his condition?
He is inside, Osman.

567
00:52:50,450 --> 00:52:51,550
All alone.

568
00:52:53,750 --> 00:52:55,950
Among all those demons.

569
00:52:56,270 --> 00:52:57,450
What if he gets exposed?

570
00:52:57,450 --> 00:52:59,450
Don't worry, brother.

571
00:52:59,720 --> 00:53:01,700
Nothing will happen.

572
00:53:02,170 --> 00:53:04,370
Be at ease.

573
00:53:05,420 --> 00:53:10,470
Aktemur is like a wolf among
dogs now.

574
00:53:14,100 --> 00:53:20,220
There is no enemy that can
deal with him.

575
00:53:20,550 --> 00:53:22,200
Don't worry.

576
00:53:29,250 --> 00:53:31,620
He is an undefeated alp,
just like his father.

577
00:53:32,670 --> 00:53:34,500
Tell me.

578
00:53:35,300 --> 00:53:38,320
What heathen ever stroke you?

579
00:53:39,500 --> 00:53:43,520
The concerns I have can't
be controlled that simply.

580
00:53:43,950 --> 00:53:45,780
I understand your concern, brother.

581
00:53:49,370 --> 00:53:51,170
Love for your children...

582
00:53:51,520 --> 00:53:53,900
is the biggest weakness a father
can have.

583
00:53:54,200 --> 00:53:56,170
And the most beautiful one.

584
00:53:56,700 --> 00:53:57,920
Remember it.

585
00:53:58,600 --> 00:54:02,350
My father Ertuğrul Ghazi loved us.

586
00:54:02,950 --> 00:54:08,250
My children, he would say.
My children are my greatest treasury.

587
00:54:09,970 --> 00:54:12,900
Then he would commit us to each other.

588
00:54:14,270 --> 00:54:15,300
Do you remember?

589
00:54:15,300 --> 00:54:16,720
Yes.

590
00:54:16,720 --> 00:54:18,720
Would I forget, brother?

591
00:54:18,720 --> 00:54:22,300
He would say, you are two branches
of a sacred three.

592
00:54:23,800 --> 00:54:29,300
And he would trust Allah and us
to protect one another.

593
00:54:30,320 --> 00:54:32,850
Brother, don't worry.

594
00:54:34,170 --> 00:54:36,570
Today is the day of conquest.

595
00:54:36,570 --> 00:54:40,600
As Allah protects us, and we protect
each other...

596
00:54:41,150 --> 00:54:43,100
Aktemur will be the same.

597
00:54:44,000 --> 00:54:46,450
Our father sow a seed to
these lands.

598
00:54:47,370 --> 00:54:48,750
We made it green.

599
00:54:49,350 --> 00:54:54,850
Inshallah, our children will make that
sycamore root to the whole world...

600
00:54:56,050 --> 00:54:59,220
with the same bravery and ambition.

601
00:55:03,920 --> 00:55:05,520
Thank you, Osman Bey.

602
00:55:05,520 --> 00:55:06,420
Thank you.

603
00:55:06,420 --> 00:55:07,970
We came for jihad.

604
00:55:07,970 --> 00:55:09,670
We lived for jihad.

605
00:55:09,670 --> 00:55:12,250
We can die happily for it.

606
00:55:14,720 --> 00:55:16,100
Give me your blessing.

607
00:55:19,070 --> 00:55:21,220
It's yours, brother.

608
00:55:21,220 --> 00:55:23,220
You too.

609
00:55:23,220 --> 00:55:25,220
It's yours.

610
00:55:36,700 --> 00:55:38,500
My pretty Holafira.

611
00:55:39,500 --> 00:55:41,630
You reminded us Mari with
your arrival...

612
00:55:41,700 --> 00:55:43,970
now your departure is harder.

613
00:55:47,150 --> 00:55:48,470
I'm sad too.

614
00:55:50,100 --> 00:55:51,820
I'm so curious about Mari.

615
00:55:51,820 --> 00:55:54,180
I wish I could listen to
her story.

616
00:55:58,000 --> 00:55:58,970
My pretty girl.

617
00:56:00,020 --> 00:56:02,000
This is your home now.

618
00:56:02,470 --> 00:56:05,520
If you don't like it there and
feel unhappy...

619
00:56:05,520 --> 00:56:07,520
our doors will always be open.

620
00:56:18,950 --> 00:56:21,200
And we'll tell you about Mari.

621
00:56:22,200 --> 00:56:24,020
She was our sister.

622
00:56:24,020 --> 00:56:25,850
And you became our daughter.

623
00:56:25,850 --> 00:56:27,370
Come again, will you?

624
00:56:32,370 --> 00:56:34,690
You are looking for my
brother Orhan, I know it.

625
00:56:34,690 --> 00:56:36,770
But he isn't good with farewells.

626
00:56:44,320 --> 00:56:46,190
Godspeed, Holafira.

627
00:56:46,870 --> 00:56:48,320
I'm grateful, Alahaddin.

628
00:56:48,920 --> 00:56:51,270
Can you tell Orhan too?

629
00:56:51,820 --> 00:56:54,450
I will, Holafira.
Godspeed.

630
00:57:13,270 --> 00:57:14,270
Holafira!

631
00:57:17,900 --> 00:57:19,120
Go in peace.

632
00:57:19,200 --> 00:57:20,510
Take care of yourself.

633
00:57:21,450 --> 00:57:22,600
Goodbye, Orhan.

634
00:57:55,400 --> 00:57:56,550
Come on, Sisters!

635
00:57:56,550 --> 00:57:58,550
We'll company the carts.

636
00:57:58,550 --> 00:58:00,550
I could send them with
the sisters.

637
00:58:01,850 --> 00:58:04,420
We should take today's provisions
with Malhun, Aygül.

638
00:58:04,420 --> 00:58:06,670
You take care of the sisters
drilling.

639
00:58:07,020 --> 00:58:09,970
Prepare them until they get
ready for battle.

640
00:58:10,120 --> 00:58:12,020
They should be ready when needed.

641
00:58:12,370 --> 00:58:15,500
Don't worry.
Don't worry.

642
00:58:15,750 --> 00:58:17,720
It's good that someone stays
in the tribe.

643
00:58:17,720 --> 00:58:20,350
We are at war.
Be cautious.

644
00:58:20,650 --> 00:58:22,470
Children are under your protection.

645
00:58:22,470 --> 00:58:25,220
Our children and tribe
are under our protection.

646
00:58:25,220 --> 00:58:27,220
Don't worry.

647
00:58:27,220 --> 00:58:29,220
Godspeed.

648
00:58:30,370 --> 00:58:31,850
Ayşe Hatun.

649
00:58:31,850 --> 00:58:34,900
The women should continue
after a rest.

650
00:58:34,900 --> 00:58:37,950
I told them but they don't
want to rest.

651
00:58:37,950 --> 00:58:40,200
They say that battle is a wedding
for the Kayı.

652
00:58:40,870 --> 00:58:42,450
We don't get tired, they say.

653
00:58:42,450 --> 00:58:45,000
Valiant women of the Kayı!
Mashallah.

654
00:58:45,000 --> 00:58:46,650
May Allah bless them.

655
00:58:46,800 --> 00:58:47,600
Inshallah.

656
00:58:49,570 --> 00:58:50,970
Come on.

657
00:58:51,700 --> 00:58:53,120
May Allah protect you.

658
00:58:54,370 --> 00:58:56,420
May Allah protect you.

659
00:58:56,420 --> 00:58:58,420
Be careful.

660
00:59:07,200 --> 00:59:08,370
Come on.

661
00:59:19,100 --> 00:59:19,950
Come on!

662
00:59:20,270 --> 00:59:21,270
Come on!

663
00:59:32,450 --> 00:59:34,370
May Allah bless our jihad.

664
00:59:39,920 --> 00:59:41,850
Amin.

665
00:59:42,900 --> 00:59:46,520
With Allah's approval,
I want to see the end of this war.

666
00:59:48,370 --> 00:59:50,100
Oh, my Ayşe.

667
00:59:50,820 --> 00:59:53,000
I understand you the best.

668
00:59:54,100 --> 00:59:58,600
I know. You think about
Aktemur.

669
00:59:59,020 --> 01:00:01,870
Your valiant is growing his renown.

670
01:00:01,950 --> 01:00:03,070
Right?

671
01:00:03,420 --> 01:00:04,850
Mashallah.

672
01:00:05,950 --> 01:00:08,600
With Allah's approval,
he'll return safe and sound.

673
01:00:08,950 --> 01:00:10,220
Inshallah, Aygül.

674
01:00:10,220 --> 01:00:12,220
Inshallah.

675
01:00:17,000 --> 01:00:17,800
My bey.

676
01:00:19,670 --> 01:00:21,000
Aktemur.

677
01:00:21,370 --> 01:00:23,250
News from Aktemur.

678
01:00:27,170 --> 01:00:29,700
Mashallah!

679
01:00:30,120 --> 01:00:31,600
Brother.

680
01:00:31,600 --> 01:00:34,070
Aktemur does his duty well.

681
01:00:34,620 --> 01:00:35,870
Be proud of your child.

682
01:00:35,870 --> 01:00:36,920
Thank you.

683
01:00:36,920 --> 01:00:38,600
Look at our valiant!

684
01:00:38,600 --> 01:00:40,600
How did he send it, Osman Bey?

685
01:01:06,770 --> 01:01:09,100
Commander Alexander.
We need to be faster.

686
01:01:09,100 --> 01:01:11,850
Commander Romanos won't like us
being late.

687
01:01:25,800 --> 01:01:29,050
I'll do many other things that Commander
Romanos won't like.

688
01:02:32,650 --> 01:02:35,000
According to my nephew Aktemur...

689
01:02:37,620 --> 01:02:42,970
Romanos will take his soldiers at Karasu
and attack us at the dawn.

690
01:02:45,050 --> 01:02:46,650
At the same time...

691
01:02:48,250 --> 01:02:51,070
Nikola will also get out of the castle
and attack us.

692
01:02:51,170 --> 01:02:53,070
They are trying to set a trap, huh?

693
01:02:53,620 --> 01:02:55,200
Let them!

694
01:02:55,250 --> 01:02:57,950
We have enough valiants
to overcome anything.

695
01:02:57,950 --> 01:02:59,950
Especially, yours, brother Gündüz!

696
01:02:59,950 --> 01:03:01,570
Mashallah to my nephew Aktemur!

697
01:03:01,570 --> 01:03:02,870
Thank you, Turgut Bey.

698
01:03:02,870 --> 01:03:04,870
Thank you.

699
01:03:05,750 --> 01:03:07,050
Osman Bey.

700
01:03:07,700 --> 01:03:10,700
This Romanos seems to be smart.

701
01:03:11,370 --> 01:03:13,950
Not many know that Karasu valley.

702
01:03:14,650 --> 01:03:16,200
My bey.

703
01:03:16,670 --> 01:03:18,970
They attack when the other tribe
beys leave.

704
01:03:20,700 --> 01:03:23,000
Then, someone leaked
information.

705
01:03:23,600 --> 01:03:26,400
Then, we have a traitor.

706
01:03:27,620 --> 01:03:33,120
As we receive intelligence,
so do they.

707
01:03:33,850 --> 01:03:35,420
We have a leak

708
01:03:36,170 --> 01:03:37,550
But...

709
01:03:37,550 --> 01:03:40,320
no one else will hear of this.

710
01:03:40,820 --> 01:03:41,920
as you order, my bey.

711
01:03:42,900 --> 01:03:45,170
According to Aktemur...

712
01:03:45,170 --> 01:03:50,200
Romanos and his soldiers will get
horses from the Rum village.

713
01:03:52,370 --> 01:03:54,500
I'll watch them with the alps.

714
01:03:56,070 --> 01:03:57,470
Turgut.

715
01:03:57,920 --> 01:03:59,000
Konur.

716
01:03:59,550 --> 01:04:04,250
You will take care of the soldiers
waiting at the valley.

717
01:04:04,850 --> 01:04:09,520
Then, we'll convince Nikola that
Romanos attacked us...

718
01:04:10,450 --> 01:04:12,170
and we'll make him leave the castle.

719
01:04:13,620 --> 01:04:16,750
It's our customs to answer traps
with traps.

720
01:04:17,970 --> 01:04:19,720
True.

721
01:04:25,720 --> 01:04:27,270
May Allah bless our jihad.

722
01:04:27,270 --> 01:04:28,450
Amin, my bey.

723
01:04:28,450 --> 01:04:29,350
Thank you!

724
01:04:31,220 --> 01:04:32,870
Come on.

725
01:04:52,300 --> 01:04:53,150
Wait.

726
01:04:53,970 --> 01:04:55,700
Follow me.
You are making a trace.

727
01:04:56,400 --> 01:04:57,470
Trackers!

728
01:04:57,550 --> 01:04:59,470
Remove all the traces!

729
01:04:59,820 --> 01:05:02,020
We left no trace, commander Romanos.

730
01:05:19,470 --> 01:05:21,690
It's the opposite of whatever
you say, Romanos.

731
01:05:21,690 --> 01:05:23,500
There will be a trace.

732
01:05:46,170 --> 01:05:47,600
Don't mess around, commander!

733
01:05:47,600 --> 01:05:49,600
You know the way.
Lead us!

734
01:05:49,720 --> 01:05:51,300
Right away, sir!

735
01:06:00,820 --> 01:06:03,280
In front of the Northern Walls

736
01:06:28,680 --> 01:06:29,720
Alps!

737
01:06:31,180 --> 01:06:32,600
What is this?

738
01:06:33,650 --> 01:06:35,340
Are you giving up?

739
01:06:36,690 --> 01:06:38,620
Conquest, we said!

740
01:06:39,320 --> 01:06:41,360
Did you think it would be easy?

741
01:06:44,210 --> 01:06:49,160
If the walls of İnegöl would go down
after a rock, it would be taken by others!

742
01:06:53,620 --> 01:06:56,500
İnegöl is the fate of the ummah!

743
01:06:58,500 --> 01:07:00,190
Don't forget, alps!

744
01:07:01,710 --> 01:07:04,290
Fate loves endeavor!

745
01:07:05,400 --> 01:07:06,860
Come on, valiants!

746
01:07:07,140 --> 01:07:09,580
I don't want any mistakes!

747
01:07:09,580 --> 01:07:10,930
Come on!

748
01:07:10,930 --> 01:07:12,470
Come on, my lions!

749
01:07:17,710 --> 01:07:19,510
Pull!

750
01:07:19,510 --> 01:07:20,830
Come on, my lions!

751
01:07:20,830 --> 01:07:24,460
Show the same ability you
have with bows!

752
01:07:24,460 --> 01:07:26,990
Pull! Pull!

753
01:07:29,760 --> 01:07:31,170
Come on, alps!

754
01:07:31,170 --> 01:07:33,590
Come on!

755
01:07:34,950 --> 01:07:36,950
Release!

756
01:07:48,670 --> 01:07:50,320
Allahu Akbar!

757
01:07:53,750 --> 01:07:56,320
Pull! Pull!

758
01:07:59,180 --> 01:08:01,330
Come on, alps!

759
01:08:02,210 --> 01:08:04,610
Release!

760
01:08:19,139 --> 01:08:20,899
You will not beat me!

761
01:08:22,139 --> 01:08:24,389
You will not beat me!

762
01:08:25,069 --> 01:08:28,950
This castle is mine!
These walls are mine!

763
01:08:34,439 --> 01:08:36,269
You will not breach it!

764
01:08:37,590 --> 01:08:39,710
You will not breach these walls!

765
01:08:50,340 --> 01:08:55,590
Sir! Sir! They keep hitting the
walls at the same spot.

766
01:08:55,590 --> 01:08:57,000
They never stop.

767
01:09:00,809 --> 01:09:02,559
Then, what will you do?

768
01:09:04,050 --> 01:09:08,700
You won't stop either!

769
01:09:08,700 --> 01:09:10,639
Did they open a hole?

770
01:09:10,639 --> 01:09:13,790
You will close that hole!

771
01:09:14,139 --> 01:09:15,519
Do you get it, soldier?

772
01:09:16,019 --> 01:09:17,250
Do you get it?

773
01:09:18,950 --> 01:09:22,370
Come on! Come on!
Come on!

774
01:09:32,660 --> 01:09:37,490
Where are you Romanos?
Where are you?

775
01:09:58,250 --> 01:10:02,780
They are removing their traces.
We need to be faster.

776
01:10:05,700 --> 01:10:06,830
Alps, faster.

777
01:10:25,890 --> 01:10:27,060
What is it, brother?

778
01:10:27,800 --> 01:10:28,900
Cerkutay?

779
01:10:29,800 --> 01:10:36,020
My bey, there are many ways and
no traces.

780
01:10:44,040 --> 01:10:50,290
Since they didn't leave a trace all the
way, they are suspicious of us.

781
01:10:53,130 --> 01:10:57,510
Alps, be cautious. It might be a trap.

782
01:11:31,280 --> 01:11:33,270
Mashallah.

783
01:11:33,690 --> 01:11:35,270
What is it, my bey?

784
01:11:37,220 --> 01:11:38,030
My nephew.

785
01:11:39,750 --> 01:11:42,800
He left a trace like my father
Ertuğrul Ghazi taught us.

786
01:11:43,820 --> 01:11:45,340
Mashallah.

787
01:11:48,930 --> 01:11:49,900
Come on.

788
01:12:15,680 --> 01:12:17,430
Did you lose the way, idiot?

789
01:12:18,210 --> 01:12:21,860
No, sir. I know these areas
very well.

790
01:12:22,570 --> 01:12:24,850
It must've felt long
because we are on foot.

791
01:12:27,110 --> 01:12:28,380
We have a missing.

792
01:12:32,830 --> 01:12:33,850
Move.

793
01:12:38,120 --> 01:12:39,120
Markus.

794
01:12:40,260 --> 01:12:41,120
Where is Markus?

795
01:12:44,250 --> 01:12:46,170
Soldiers, haven't anyone seen
Markus?

796
01:12:46,470 --> 01:12:48,840
We haven't, sir. He was at
the end of the line.

797
01:12:53,220 --> 01:12:54,140
You!

798
01:12:58,280 --> 01:13:00,590
Markus was coming with you.
Didn't you see him?

799
01:13:01,800 --> 01:13:04,930
No, sir. It's been a long time
since he left me.

800
01:13:05,340 --> 01:13:06,840
I thought he went forward.

801
01:13:09,480 --> 01:13:11,000
Where did this man go?

802
01:13:13,630 --> 01:13:16,640
Sir, there is no time to search.

803
01:13:18,170 --> 01:13:19,470
Maybe he fled.

804
01:13:37,770 --> 01:13:40,120
No news from Commander Romanos.

805
01:13:40,490 --> 01:13:43,580
Commander wanted us to wait.
He'll come.

806
01:13:44,400 --> 01:13:46,780
I can't wait to spill Turkish blood.

807
01:14:02,180 --> 01:14:03,840
They have the numbers.

808
01:14:05,410 --> 01:14:09,150
We'll get the spotters with
arrows first.

809
01:14:09,150 --> 01:14:11,470
Then, we'll attack altogether.

810
01:14:13,620 --> 01:14:17,190
If Allah allows, we'll
destroy them, alps.

811
01:14:17,670 --> 01:14:18,930
Inshallah, Turgut Bey.

812
01:14:19,590 --> 01:14:21,380
We won't let anyone survive.

813
01:14:21,970 --> 01:14:23,670
We'll attack from the rear, Kutan.

814
01:14:23,810 --> 01:14:24,900
Alright, my bey.

815
01:14:25,180 --> 01:14:27,720
You know what to do when
you see the signal.

816
01:14:28,040 --> 01:14:31,900
We'll fight to the death.
May Allah bless our jihad.

817
01:14:31,900 --> 01:14:32,790
Amin.

818
01:14:33,300 --> 01:14:35,550
Alps. We'll go forward.

819
01:14:35,810 --> 01:14:36,820
Come on.

820
01:14:50,650 --> 01:14:53,060
I'm sorry for calling you an idiot.

821
01:14:54,240 --> 01:14:56,290
It's not important,
Commander Romanos.

822
01:14:56,570 --> 01:15:00,190
We are at war. We shouldn't be bothered
by such little things.

823
01:15:01,000 --> 01:15:01,820
True.

824
01:15:03,560 --> 01:15:05,750
How long how you been
in Bilecik Castle.

825
01:15:06,040 --> 01:15:11,790
A year ago, I was sent by the Emperor's
regent to learn about Bilecik.

826
01:15:13,190 --> 01:15:15,740
But before I get to learn,
Osman captured me.

827
01:15:17,060 --> 01:15:19,410
Then, it was Regent Pericles.

828
01:15:39,870 --> 01:15:40,950
Be careful.

829
01:15:44,320 --> 01:15:46,150
He is a very dangerous man.

830
01:15:48,430 --> 01:15:49,890
You shouldn't trust him.

831
01:15:58,230 --> 01:16:00,440
Pericles wasn't the regent a year ago!

832
01:16:00,560 --> 01:16:03,260
You are a traitor! You are a traitor!

833
01:16:25,240 --> 01:16:26,640
Osman is following us.

834
01:16:28,900 --> 01:16:32,150
Wait here and use this fool
as a bait.

835
01:16:32,950 --> 01:16:35,570
You. You.
You will come with me.

836
01:16:35,570 --> 01:16:37,060
We have no time to waste.

837
01:16:37,770 --> 01:16:40,810
Don't come with me before
you kill them all.

838
01:17:15,550 --> 01:17:20,440
Don't be sad, brother. Allah knows it,
maybe you'll see her again.

839
01:17:22,110 --> 01:17:24,840
I was sad that you wouldn't
say farewell to her.

840
01:17:24,950 --> 01:17:26,440
But you came in time.

841
01:17:28,710 --> 01:17:32,120
You know it, brother. I'm not
good with farewells.

842
01:17:32,700 --> 01:17:34,420
I know, brother.
I know.

843
01:17:34,990 --> 01:17:38,760
Holafira understands it.
She sent her regards.

844
01:17:41,610 --> 01:17:42,380
Alahaddin.

845
01:17:44,480 --> 01:17:45,840
I'm glad to have you.

846
01:17:46,470 --> 01:17:48,640
Who would support me if
not for you?

847
01:17:49,140 --> 01:17:52,250
Don't let our other brothers
hear that and get jealous.

848
01:17:53,030 --> 01:17:54,660
Don't tell them, brother.

849
01:17:55,180 --> 01:17:57,020
It's enough for two of us
to know.

850
01:17:57,020 --> 01:17:58,420
Alright, brother.

851
01:18:06,270 --> 01:18:08,970
The guest girl dropped her
necklace in the tent.

852
01:18:15,960 --> 01:18:17,090
Alahaddin.

853
01:18:18,260 --> 01:18:20,160
This is Holafira's mother's necklace.

854
01:18:20,700 --> 01:18:23,590
-Why would she leave it?
-She must've forgotten it, brother.

855
01:18:35,800 --> 01:18:40,410
It has sentimental value.
She will be sad.

856
01:18:43,740 --> 01:18:44,480
Brother.

857
01:18:46,270 --> 01:18:48,840
You won't follow her because
of a necklace, will you?

858
01:18:49,570 --> 01:18:52,400
My father will find a way when
he returns.

859
01:19:31,340 --> 01:19:32,130
Come on!

860
01:19:50,160 --> 01:19:51,140
My shehzad.

861
01:19:52,710 --> 01:19:54,950
You scared me, Baysungur Alp.

862
01:19:55,320 --> 01:19:57,970
What are you doing here? Where is
your brother?

863
01:19:57,970 --> 01:19:59,910
You were supposed to be training

864
01:20:06,660 --> 01:20:10,670
Alright, then. Find your brother.
Get your weapons and come to drill.

865
01:20:11,310 --> 01:20:14,120
We'll come after I find my brother.
Inshallah.

866
01:20:19,350 --> 01:20:20,880
Oh, brother, oh.

867
01:20:21,580 --> 01:20:24,400
I almost lied because of you.

868
01:20:49,430 --> 01:20:51,950
With the name of Allah.

869
01:21:10,080 --> 01:21:12,210
Come on! Come on!

870
01:21:26,240 --> 01:21:28,090
You won't succeed!

871
01:21:28,520 --> 01:21:30,920
Osman Bey will send you all to hell!

872
01:21:31,230 --> 01:21:33,580
You will go there before us, Turk.

873
01:21:37,180 --> 01:21:38,230
My nephew!

874
01:21:42,110 --> 01:21:44,100
Romanos got him.

875
01:21:44,730 --> 01:21:47,740
Alps. Be cautious.

876
01:21:50,330 --> 01:21:52,010
This might be a trap.

877
01:21:55,890 --> 01:21:57,580
You know what to do.

878
01:22:03,240 --> 01:22:04,180
Come on.

879
01:22:16,040 --> 01:22:17,610
Boran. Take him out.

880
01:22:17,610 --> 01:22:18,610
Yes, my bey.

881
01:22:30,030 --> 01:22:31,360
-My nephew.
-My bey.

882
01:22:32,960 --> 01:22:34,930
-Are you alright?
-I am, my bey.

883
01:22:41,450 --> 01:22:44,770
Brothers, archer formation!

884
01:23:08,910 --> 01:23:09,820
Come on.

885
01:23:13,400 --> 01:23:17,080
My bey, Romanos is going to his
soldiers at the valley.

886
01:23:20,230 --> 01:23:23,110
Alps. Go to the valley.

887
01:23:24,860 --> 01:23:26,660
I'll go after Romanos.

888
01:23:27,290 --> 01:23:28,480
As you order, my bey.

889
01:23:29,010 --> 01:23:29,900
My nephew.

890
01:23:31,980 --> 01:23:34,170
My Aktemur.
Are you alright?

891
01:23:34,170 --> 01:23:37,390
Thank you, Boran Alp.
My father was right about you.

892
01:23:38,340 --> 01:23:39,590
Mashallah.

893
01:23:39,910 --> 01:23:43,940
Brothers, we are going to the valley.
Come on!

894
01:23:48,840 --> 01:23:52,430
Come on, alps!
It's time to keep our word to Osman Bey!

895
01:23:52,980 --> 01:23:57,900
Allah is righteous!

896
01:24:57,700 --> 01:24:59,700
Where are you going, Romanos?

897
01:25:01,500 --> 01:25:03,140
Are you in a hurry?

898
01:25:04,680 --> 01:25:06,060
So, you found me.

899
01:25:06,780 --> 01:25:11,520
Are you going to your soldiers
at the valley?

900
01:25:13,700 --> 01:25:15,880
Do you think that you still
have soldiers.

901
01:25:17,760 --> 01:25:21,340
Do you think that I would
come here with a bunch of soldiers?

902
01:25:23,460 --> 01:25:25,680
I'm not like those lords.

903
01:25:28,340 --> 01:25:31,500
I'm not like anyone.

904
01:25:33,500 --> 01:25:34,980
Attack.

905
01:26:08,780 --> 01:26:11,120
Run, Romanos.
Run.

906
01:26:11,760 --> 01:26:13,640
Where are you running to?

907
01:26:15,100 --> 01:26:17,580
Who did ever get away
from me?

908
01:26:42,840 --> 01:26:45,020
Where are you?

909
01:26:45,380 --> 01:26:48,500
My Allah, watch over my brother.

910
01:26:50,740 --> 01:26:51,500
Come on!

911
01:27:16,800 --> 01:27:18,760
Kayı Tribe declared war on İnegöl, sir.

912
01:27:19,880 --> 01:27:23,540
We poisoned the provisions to the quarters
instead of the tribe.

913
01:27:26,120 --> 01:27:28,080
They aren't my aunt's soldiers.

914
01:27:30,280 --> 01:27:32,140
I must inform the tribe at once.

915
01:27:33,780 --> 01:27:35,220
Where is Master Darius?

916
01:27:35,410 --> 01:27:37,770
We were supposed to talk to him.

917
01:27:38,340 --> 01:27:40,700
Master Darius died.
Osman killed him.

918
01:27:41,260 --> 01:27:42,800
How could this happen?

919
01:27:43,020 --> 01:27:45,760
What are we waiting for?

920
01:27:46,160 --> 01:27:48,600
Let's burn Kayı Tribe!
Leave no living there!

921
01:27:48,600 --> 01:27:50,180
She is running away!

922
01:27:50,180 --> 01:27:52,560
Hurry! Follow her!

923
01:28:13,020 --> 01:28:14,620
Stop! Don't run!

924
01:28:23,100 --> 01:28:26,860
They'll kill Osman Bey's soldiers.

925
01:28:44,920 --> 01:28:46,380
-Holafira!
-Orhan!

926
01:28:53,990 --> 01:28:55,990
What's happening here?

927
01:28:56,210 --> 01:28:59,660
They aren't my aunt's soldiers.

928
01:29:00,800 --> 01:29:01,980
Your enemies.

929
01:29:05,720 --> 01:29:07,180
Hide behind me!

930
01:29:18,400 --> 01:29:20,440
Ya Allah!

931
01:29:22,440 --> 01:29:23,440
I'm here, brother.

932
01:29:26,300 --> 01:29:27,740
My valiant brother.

933
01:29:35,380 --> 01:29:38,660
They poisoned the provisions
going to the alps.

934
01:29:38,920 --> 01:29:40,660
We must inform them.

935
01:29:40,760 --> 01:29:43,900
If we can't get there in time,
we'll lose the siege.

936
01:29:43,900 --> 01:29:47,160
Alahaddin, inform our mothers.

937
01:29:47,800 --> 01:29:49,460
I won't leave you, brother.

938
01:29:49,460 --> 01:29:51,840
Brother, go and inform our mothers.

939
01:30:02,910 --> 01:30:04,130
Where are those?

940
01:30:22,660 --> 01:30:26,080
You will be the guarantee of my exit
From these cursed Turkish lands

941
01:30:26,240 --> 01:30:28,480
Only your corpse will
get out of this land!

942
01:30:29,280 --> 01:30:30,840
Take him!

943
01:30:33,840 --> 01:30:37,430
Don't be afraid, neither father
nor mother will leave us here.

944
01:30:37,915 --> 01:30:39,745
Alaeddin will catch up.

945
01:30:41,670 --> 01:30:43,740
I know.
I am not afraid.

946
01:31:15,840 --> 01:31:17,340
Brothers!

947
01:31:20,320 --> 01:31:22,820
Romanos escaped...

948
01:31:23,460 --> 01:31:25,580
...but he cannot go back to
the castle like that.

949
01:31:26,620 --> 01:31:28,520
Nikola's plan is wasted.

950
01:31:30,720 --> 01:31:32,520
His time is over.

951
01:31:33,760 --> 01:31:35,560
It's our turn now.

952
01:31:37,720 --> 01:31:38,820
Right now...

953
01:31:40,080 --> 01:31:42,760
The catapults headed by Gündüz Bey...

954
01:31:43,200 --> 01:31:45,360
...strike the castle walls
day and night.

955
01:31:46,860 --> 01:31:52,300
But, we will not wait for a breach.

956
01:31:53,780 --> 01:31:55,100
Aktemur.

957
01:31:55,600 --> 01:31:58,260
You will enter the castle
with a couple alps.

958
01:31:59,100 --> 01:32:01,920
You will say Romanos will
attack us before sunrise.

959
01:32:02,780 --> 01:32:07,000
Nikola will leave the castle with his
soldiers after hearing this.

960
01:32:07,820 --> 01:32:11,160
The rest will kill Nikola and his soldiers.

961
01:32:12,480 --> 01:32:18,920
In that case, my nephew Aktemur
will break the bridges and open the gates.

962
01:32:19,700 --> 01:32:21,750
Inshallah,(If Allah permits)
Turgut Bey.

963
01:32:22,280 --> 01:32:23,780
This is our aim.

964
01:32:24,160 --> 01:32:27,020
But we will still be cautious.

965
01:32:27,180 --> 01:32:30,680
Because when the bridges are open...

966
01:32:31,380 --> 01:32:33,400
They'll notice Aktemur.

967
01:32:34,200 --> 01:32:36,420
When Aktemur gives us the sign...

968
01:32:37,620 --> 01:32:39,700
...we'll break the gates
with battering jam.

969
01:32:40,980 --> 01:32:41,920
My Bey.

970
01:32:42,840 --> 01:32:46,600
What is going to happen to Aktemur
and his alps in that case?

971
01:32:48,320 --> 01:32:50,000
Gunduz Bey is worried
about this too.

972
01:32:50,340 --> 01:32:53,580
That's why he will place
stairs...

973
01:32:53,880 --> 01:32:56,180
...climb up to the castle
and attack.

974
01:32:56,740 --> 01:32:58,960
After he attracts
Nikola and his soldiers...

975
01:32:59,940 --> 01:33:02,480
...the bridge and gates will
be open for us.

976
01:33:06,560 --> 01:33:08,780
We will not leave Aktemur alone.

977
01:33:11,300 --> 01:33:14,440
My Bey, who are the alps
to join Aktemur?

978
01:33:14,440 --> 01:33:19,280
My Bey, if you will excuse us, we want to
enter the castle with our brother Aktemur.

979
01:33:19,480 --> 01:33:22,920
We'll open the bridge and the gates,
even if it costs our lives, my Bey.

980
01:33:22,920 --> 01:33:24,560
We want this mission.

981
01:33:28,040 --> 01:33:29,110
Eyvallah.
(Thank you)

982
01:33:30,820 --> 01:33:31,860
Eyvallah.
(Thank you)

983
01:33:32,720 --> 01:33:35,960
So wear your equipments!

984
01:33:36,020 --> 01:33:38,250
- As you order, my Bey.
- As you order, my Bey.

985
01:33:40,220 --> 01:33:42,980
We pounced on Ingul like a claw

986
01:33:44,340 --> 01:33:45,900
From behind the walls

987
01:33:46,120 --> 01:33:49,200
And from above
and from the gates

988
01:33:49,360 --> 01:33:50,860
and behind the gates!

989
01:33:52,100 --> 01:33:54,020
We will attack from all sides!

990
01:33:54,320 --> 01:33:56,020
It is time to slaughter!

991
01:33:56,600 --> 01:33:58,020
Alps!

992
01:34:01,920 --> 01:34:03,080
Come on.

993
01:34:17,660 --> 01:34:18,640
Mother!

994
01:34:19,180 --> 01:34:20,640
Stop, mother!

995
01:34:21,220 --> 01:34:23,880
Alaeddin!
Son!

996
01:34:28,950 --> 01:34:31,460
Son, what's it?
What is it?

997
01:34:31,680 --> 01:34:33,860
Mother, my mother!

998
01:34:34,440 --> 01:34:37,580
Alaeddin, son!
What happened? Where is Orhan?

999
01:34:37,580 --> 01:34:38,680
Tell me.

1000
01:34:38,920 --> 01:34:42,280
They might have kidnapped
my brother Orhan and Holoferi.

1001
01:34:43,020 --> 01:34:44,790
What are you talking about Alaeddin?

1002
01:34:44,800 --> 01:34:47,000
Who kidnapped Orhan and why?

1003
01:34:47,160 --> 01:34:50,760
The ones who came to get Holoferi
were not her aunt's men, mother.

1004
01:34:50,980 --> 01:34:52,540
They were enemy.

1005
01:34:56,460 --> 01:34:59,000
They poisoned the provisions
of alps.

1006
01:35:00,680 --> 01:35:05,920
Ignobles! They can't dare to duel,
they try poisoning!

1007
01:35:06,440 --> 01:35:08,040
Save my brother, mother.

1008
01:35:08,040 --> 01:35:11,740
He is alone.
They might have been kidnapped.

1009
01:35:13,060 --> 01:35:14,660
We will save them, son.

1010
01:35:14,920 --> 01:35:16,660
We will save your brother.

1011
01:35:20,620 --> 01:35:23,410
Kumral Abdal, destroy the provisions.

1012
01:35:23,480 --> 01:35:26,120
Go and inform the quarters
with sisters.

1013
01:35:26,760 --> 01:35:28,380
My Alaeddin is entrusted to you.

1014
01:35:28,620 --> 01:35:31,340
We will go to save Orhan
with Baysungur Alp.

1015
01:35:32,180 --> 01:35:33,340
Don't worry.

1016
01:35:36,520 --> 01:35:38,120
Baysungur Alp!

1017
01:35:40,280 --> 01:35:42,020
Come, my valiant.

1018
01:35:44,220 --> 01:35:46,720
Come on now!

1019
01:35:48,120 --> 01:35:49,100
Go!

1020
01:35:49,180 --> 01:35:49,900
Selvi!

1021
01:35:51,560 --> 01:35:54,460
Barkin!
Barkin, you came just in time.

1022
01:35:54,520 --> 01:35:56,720
Selvi, what's happening here?

1023
01:35:57,240 --> 01:35:58,560
Where are the Hatuns going?

1024
01:35:58,560 --> 01:36:02,480
They went to save Orhan. The ones who came
for Holofire turned out to be enemies.

1025
01:36:04,200 --> 01:36:06,420
- Husamettin!
- My Bey!

1026
01:36:06,540 --> 01:36:09,240
Take Alps and deploy
where Osman Bey told you to.

1027
01:36:10,400 --> 01:36:12,360
We'll go to Hatuns with Selvi.

1028
01:36:13,580 --> 01:36:14,360
Come.

1029
01:36:30,540 --> 01:36:32,880
Sisters, dig a hole.

1030
01:36:33,560 --> 01:36:35,460
Bury the poisonous provisions.

1031
01:36:36,240 --> 01:36:38,920
Hurry.
Hurry.

1032
01:36:44,980 --> 01:36:48,200
Pull pull pull pull!

1033
01:36:51,540 --> 01:36:52,620
Straighten it!

1034
01:36:56,060 --> 01:36:58,200
Come on lions!

1035
01:37:01,680 --> 01:37:03,740
O Haqq!

1036
01:37:15,060 --> 01:37:16,640
Allah is the greatest!

1037
01:37:16,790 --> 01:37:18,060
Allah is the greatest!

1038
01:37:18,060 --> 01:37:20,400
Come on come on come on!

1039
01:37:33,820 --> 01:37:35,360
Allah is the greatest!

1040
01:37:36,600 --> 01:37:38,200
Allah is the greatest!

1041
01:37:39,860 --> 01:37:42,350
Allah is the greatest!

1042
01:37:57,860 --> 01:37:59,340
Come on.

1043
01:38:26,840 --> 01:38:30,040
Allah is the greatest!

1044
01:38:30,120 --> 01:38:32,680
Run!
Inform Lord Nikola!

1045
01:38:33,020 --> 01:38:35,560
The walls are crunching!

1046
01:38:38,340 --> 01:38:39,620
Come on valiants!

1047
01:38:39,860 --> 01:38:41,620
Come on lions!

1048
01:38:42,100 --> 01:38:43,960
Come on valiants!

1049
01:38:44,220 --> 01:38:45,960
Come on!

1050
01:38:46,420 --> 01:38:47,960
Come on!

1051
01:38:57,600 --> 01:38:58,760
Speak up!

1052
01:38:58,760 --> 01:39:01,280
Sir, the north walls are
demolished heavily.

1053
01:39:01,460 --> 01:39:02,540
They are cracking.

1054
01:39:05,200 --> 01:39:07,100
They shall not crack!

1055
01:39:08,400 --> 01:39:09,620
Do you understand?

1056
01:39:10,540 --> 01:39:13,960
If the walls crack, army cracks.

1057
01:39:13,960 --> 01:39:16,720
If army cracks, we crack!

1058
01:39:16,720 --> 01:39:18,720
Do you understand me!?

1059
01:39:19,340 --> 01:39:23,000
If that happens,
I will not let Osman's alps to kill you.

1060
01:39:24,060 --> 01:39:25,880
I will strangle you with my hands!

1061
01:39:26,080 --> 01:39:27,720
With my hands!

1062
01:39:27,980 --> 01:39:30,200
Get out.
Get out!

1063
01:39:30,880 --> 01:39:32,580
Get out all!

1064
01:39:47,500 --> 01:39:49,880
This castle will not fall.

1065
01:39:52,700 --> 01:39:55,040
It will not fall.

1066
01:40:01,680 --> 01:40:02,820
Osman.

1067
01:40:03,680 --> 01:40:05,780
Death will be your escape...

1068
01:40:06,140 --> 01:40:08,560
...after what I do to you!

1069
01:40:17,620 --> 01:40:20,300
Come on now.
Come to me.

1070
01:40:22,040 --> 01:40:23,180
Come to me.

1071
01:40:34,160 --> 01:40:36,540
Are you all Osman could send?

1072
01:40:37,080 --> 01:40:38,540
Osman?

1073
01:40:39,520 --> 01:40:42,680
No sir. I am not Osman's man.
I am his enemy.

1074
01:40:43,440 --> 01:40:46,800
You must be one of the
Rome commanders.

1075
01:40:48,140 --> 01:40:49,340
Right.

1076
01:40:50,260 --> 01:40:51,820
But you are missing.

1077
01:40:53,020 --> 01:40:59,400
I am the most famous, the most relentless
commander Romanus!

1078
01:41:02,620 --> 01:41:03,670
What about you?

1079
01:41:04,200 --> 01:41:05,640
Osman's enemy.

1080
01:41:06,220 --> 01:41:07,640
Who are you?

1081
01:41:08,320 --> 01:41:09,640
Who is your name?

1082
01:41:10,140 --> 01:41:12,160
How can I be sure?

1083
01:41:12,260 --> 01:41:16,380
I was Master Arius' closest man,
may God bless him.

1084
01:41:16,620 --> 01:41:18,380
My real name is Aizek.

1085
01:41:18,800 --> 01:41:20,060
Arius.

1086
01:41:21,740 --> 01:41:24,540
I saw his head in a bag.

1087
01:41:27,020 --> 01:41:30,440
Aizek,
Aizek, Aizek, Aizek, Aizek.

1088
01:41:40,500 --> 01:41:43,640
A sign that only Arius' men carry.

1089
01:41:49,680 --> 01:41:51,500
So you are on my side.

1090
01:41:52,640 --> 01:41:54,380
I forget my friends.

1091
01:41:56,040 --> 01:41:58,280
But I never forget my enemies.

1092
01:42:02,280 --> 01:42:03,460
Osman.

1093
01:42:06,020 --> 01:42:08,640
I will never forget his face.

1094
01:42:10,320 --> 01:42:13,460
I will make him pay for all the
things he did to us!

1095
01:42:14,920 --> 01:42:17,220
I don't know how long I'll live,
Commander Romanus.

1096
01:42:17,460 --> 01:42:19,220
But I swear that...

1097
01:42:19,500 --> 01:42:22,160
I'll avenge for Master Arius before I die.

1098
01:42:22,300 --> 01:42:25,540
And I will serve for his case.

1099
01:42:26,220 --> 01:42:27,760
Flare your hatred.

1100
01:42:28,440 --> 01:42:33,080
You will be with me while I skin Osman !

1101
01:42:33,320 --> 01:42:35,660
I can't wait to see that moment, sir.

1102
01:43:17,340 --> 01:43:19,260
May our war be blessed.

1103
01:43:20,420 --> 01:43:21,680
Eyvallah.

1104
01:43:32,160 --> 01:43:34,580
Come on!
Pull!

1105
01:43:34,580 --> 01:43:36,840
Allah is the greatest!

1106
01:43:38,020 --> 01:43:40,120
Pull pull pull pull!

1107
01:43:40,260 --> 01:43:42,680
Come on!
Come on!

1108
01:43:42,680 --> 01:43:44,820
Pull pull pull pull!

1109
01:43:44,820 --> 01:43:46,000
Come on brother!

1110
01:43:47,680 --> 01:43:48,980
Throw!

1111
01:44:12,450 --> 01:44:16,950
Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest!

1112
01:44:17,650 --> 01:44:20,100
Come on my valiants!

1113
01:44:20,100 --> 01:44:22,420
Come on valiants!
Come on alps!

1114
01:44:22,420 --> 01:44:25,870
Pull pull pull!
Come on!

1115
01:44:30,320 --> 01:44:31,470
Cerkutay.

1116
01:44:31,470 --> 01:44:33,410
That castle will be conquered tonight!

1117
01:44:33,470 --> 01:44:35,270
Come on, come on!

1118
01:44:35,950 --> 01:44:37,550
Come on valiants!

1119
01:44:40,850 --> 01:44:43,270
Remember the promise we gave to Osman Bey!

1120
01:44:43,270 --> 01:44:45,270
Come on!

1121
01:44:50,900 --> 01:44:54,320
Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest!

1122
01:44:54,740 --> 01:44:56,320
Throw!

1123
01:44:56,320 --> 01:44:57,620
Allah is the greatest!

1124
01:45:07,220 --> 01:45:09,450
Help!

1125
01:45:10,550 --> 01:45:12,000
Allah is the greatest!

1126
01:45:23,000 --> 01:45:24,700
Allah is the greatest!

1127
01:45:24,850 --> 01:45:28,320
Masha Allah! (praise be!)
Masha Allah! (praise be!)

1128
01:45:28,450 --> 01:45:32,900
As long as we have that much brave men,
we will not leave any unconquered castle!

1129
01:45:32,900 --> 01:45:36,320
This is what Ertugrul Ghazi's son can do!

1130
01:45:36,320 --> 01:45:39,970
We learned from the master,
from you Master Davut!

1131
01:45:39,970 --> 01:45:41,970
- Eyvallah! (thank you)
- Welcome!

1132
01:45:43,400 --> 01:45:44,800
Throw!

1133
01:45:45,800 --> 01:45:47,270
Allah is eternal!

1134
01:45:55,320 --> 01:45:57,320
Come on!

1135
01:45:57,320 --> 01:45:59,320
Come on valiants!

1136
01:46:00,700 --> 01:46:03,000
Come on pull!
Pull pull pull pull!

1137
01:46:04,550 --> 01:46:06,650
Back!

1138
01:46:20,850 --> 01:46:22,850
Now!

1139
01:46:23,020 --> 01:46:25,150
You came with luck, Master Davut!

1140
01:46:25,150 --> 01:46:27,350
- Masha Allah! (praise be)
- Thank Allah!

1141
01:46:27,350 --> 01:46:31,970
Allah is the greatest!

1142
01:46:31,970 --> 01:46:33,770
O Allah's Muhammed!

1143
01:46:33,770 --> 01:46:45,570
Allah is the greatest!

1144
01:46:45,570 --> 01:46:48,050
We saw that they are not indestructible.

1145
01:46:48,050 --> 01:46:50,050
Thank Allah.

1146
01:46:50,270 --> 01:46:52,800
Prepare Kayi flags, alps!

1147
01:46:52,800 --> 01:46:54,150
Time has come.

1148
01:46:54,150 --> 01:46:56,050
Inshallah Konur, Inshallah!

1149
01:46:56,050 --> 01:46:57,650
We attacked the first.

1150
01:46:57,650 --> 01:46:59,370
Our path is open now.

1151
01:46:59,370 --> 01:47:02,200
Our path is open thanks to Allah!

1152
01:47:06,700 --> 01:47:10,250
Konur, Boran, time to attack.

1153
01:47:10,970 --> 01:47:12,520
Aktemur is inside.

1154
01:47:12,530 --> 01:47:15,790
This attack is a gift for me, Boran!

1155
01:47:15,800 --> 01:47:18,470
You'll kill the infidels of Nikola
in there.

1156
01:47:18,470 --> 01:47:20,700
- Come on my valiants.
- As you order, my Bey.

1157
01:47:20,700 --> 01:47:22,370
As you order, Gunduz Bey.

1158
01:47:24,050 --> 01:47:25,310
What about me, my Bey?

1159
01:47:25,310 --> 01:47:27,570
Your place is my side, Cerkutay!

1160
01:47:27,570 --> 01:47:29,270
My side!

1161
01:47:29,270 --> 01:47:30,670
Eyvallah my Bey!

1162
01:47:30,670 --> 01:47:33,370
Tell us to break, tell us to destroy!

1163
01:47:33,370 --> 01:47:35,050
Destroy, Cerkutay!

1164
01:47:35,050 --> 01:47:37,050
Let's make a breach!
Break them!

1165
01:47:37,050 --> 01:47:37,820
Come on!

1166
01:47:37,820 --> 01:47:41,250
So what we need to do
is to make a breach.

1167
01:47:41,250 --> 01:47:43,250
Come on! Come on!

1168
01:47:44,320 --> 01:47:46,100
Come on! Come on!

1169
01:47:47,300 --> 01:47:49,470
O Haqq!

1170
01:47:50,250 --> 01:47:53,900
Praise be!
Praise be!

1171
01:47:54,470 --> 01:47:57,450
My Bey, this is for you!

1172
01:47:57,450 --> 01:47:59,450
Fill it!

1173
01:47:59,450 --> 01:48:01,450
Come on my lion!

1174
01:48:08,000 --> 01:48:10,470
Back!

1175
01:48:10,900 --> 01:48:12,050
Come on!

1176
01:48:12,700 --> 01:48:14,070
O Haqq!

1177
01:48:29,150 --> 01:48:32,720
Allah is the greatest!

1178
01:48:35,470 --> 01:48:37,670
Praise be!

1179
01:48:37,670 --> 01:48:40,120
My Bey, this one is yours.

1180
01:48:43,550 --> 01:48:46,300
O Haqq!

1181
01:48:49,870 --> 01:48:58,250
Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest!

1182
01:48:58,250 --> 01:49:00,250
Allah is the greatest!

1183
01:49:05,570 --> 01:49:07,100
Come on Alps.

1184
01:49:07,670 --> 01:49:10,320
We'll shoot our arrows and never stop.

1185
01:49:12,100 --> 01:49:13,820
In the name of Allah.

1186
01:49:24,950 --> 01:49:26,270
Who are you?

1187
01:49:29,020 --> 01:49:30,420
I am Alexander.

1188
01:49:31,270 --> 01:49:33,820
I brought news from Commander Romanus.

1189
01:49:41,470 --> 01:49:42,350
Now.

1190
01:49:55,380 --> 01:49:58,600
Open the bridge!
Turks are after us!

1191
01:50:01,600 --> 01:50:02,550
Now.

1192
01:50:06,300 --> 01:50:08,220
Come on open the gates!

1193
01:50:08,870 --> 01:50:10,220
Open the gates!

1194
01:50:58,500 --> 01:50:59,870
Come on Alps!

1195
01:51:35,050 --> 01:51:37,020
How is the situation?

1196
01:51:37,170 --> 01:51:41,000
They took the bait.

1197
01:51:41,520 --> 01:51:44,070
The gates are open for Aktemur, Osman Bey.

1198
01:51:44,700 --> 01:51:47,400
Eyvallah, eyvallah.

1199
01:51:48,900 --> 01:51:51,950
Praise be to Aktemur.

1200
01:51:51,950 --> 01:51:53,950
Praise be so.

1201
01:51:56,170 --> 01:51:58,750
We have been waiting for this moment for
a long time.

1202
01:51:59,800 --> 01:52:01,770
We have been through a lot.

1203
01:52:02,300 --> 01:52:04,250
Thank Allah, we managed.

1204
01:52:04,920 --> 01:52:07,770
We are closer to the infidels
than their breath, Osman Bey.

1205
01:52:08,900 --> 01:52:13,750
Turkmen Beys are blinded outside
because they are always busy inside.

1206
01:52:15,150 --> 01:52:16,900
But you are not like that.

1207
01:52:18,500 --> 01:52:20,150
You always backed me up.

1208
01:52:24,600 --> 01:52:26,150
The path is tough.

1209
01:52:27,820 --> 01:52:31,100
But your brotherhood is tougher.

1210
01:52:31,520 --> 01:52:32,750
Thank you.

1211
01:52:34,500 --> 01:52:36,170
I was bull-headed, Osman Bey.

1212
01:52:37,820 --> 01:52:39,400
You taught me how to unite.

1213
01:52:41,300 --> 01:52:42,670
Now I know...

1214
01:52:43,400 --> 01:52:47,550
...as long as we are united,
we'll break every gates.

1215
01:52:48,450 --> 01:52:50,750
We'll proceed like a battering ram.

1216
01:52:51,950 --> 01:52:52,950
I know it now.

1217
01:52:54,770 --> 01:52:57,120
Turks will not rest from now on.

1218
01:52:58,120 --> 01:53:00,250
We are on a path where...

1219
01:53:00,950 --> 01:53:04,970
...you fall behind if you don't
force yourself to proceed.

1220
01:53:05,200 --> 01:53:06,400
Then...

1221
01:53:07,120 --> 01:53:09,180
...we'll always go forward, Osman Bey!

1222
01:53:12,850 --> 01:53:15,050
Always go forward.

1223
01:53:28,550 --> 01:53:31,550
You came this far, Kumral Abdal.
What's the problem?

1224
01:53:31,970 --> 01:53:34,600
The enemy is inside the tribe, Osman Bey.

1225
01:53:34,800 --> 01:53:36,920
They poisoned the provisions of Alps.

1226
01:53:37,550 --> 01:53:39,570
What are you saying, Kumral Abdal?

1227
01:53:40,050 --> 01:53:41,300
Where are the Hatuns?

1228
01:53:41,850 --> 01:53:43,800
What is Alaeddin doing here?

1229
01:53:44,250 --> 01:53:45,270
My Bey...

1230
01:53:45,270 --> 01:53:48,220
...my brother and Holofira are
kidnapped by the enemy.

1231
01:53:51,500 --> 01:53:53,270
Don't worry, nephew.

1232
01:53:53,270 --> 01:53:55,270
We'll have them back safe and sound.

1233
01:53:56,820 --> 01:54:00,400
Alaeddin informed us.
Bala Hatun sent us here.

1234
01:54:00,420 --> 01:54:02,070
We destroyed the poisonous
provisions.

1235
01:54:02,400 --> 01:54:04,850
Hatuns and Barkin Bey
went after Orhan.

1236
01:54:06,320 --> 01:54:09,970
Alaeddin, go rest, nephew.

1237
01:54:09,970 --> 01:54:11,970
As you command, uncle.

1238
01:54:13,620 --> 01:54:15,250
Come on.

1239
01:54:32,750 --> 01:54:34,050
Alexander?

1240
01:54:34,670 --> 01:54:36,670
We did it, Lord Nikola!

1241
01:54:38,170 --> 01:54:40,170
Commander Romanos got his troop.

1242
01:54:40,170 --> 01:54:41,600
This is good news!

1243
01:54:41,620 --> 01:54:44,500
Listen to me.
This is some good news, Alexander!

1244
01:54:44,500 --> 01:54:46,500
Commander Romanos wanted me to inform you.

1245
01:54:46,750 --> 01:54:50,270
They are waiting for the troops of castle
to attack the quarters.

1246
01:54:50,270 --> 01:54:52,270
Everything is going by your plan.

1247
01:54:52,950 --> 01:54:56,070
We are not going to wait any longer.
We will act immediately!

1248
01:54:56,070 --> 01:54:57,150
Now!

1249
01:54:57,150 --> 01:54:59,150
Yes sir.

1250
01:54:59,370 --> 01:55:00,700
Hurry.

1251
01:55:01,420 --> 01:55:02,670
Hurry.

1252
01:55:05,450 --> 01:55:07,220
Hurry.

1253
01:55:13,070 --> 01:55:14,700
Good.

1254
01:55:22,750 --> 01:55:24,170
My Bey.

1255
01:55:24,180 --> 01:55:26,460
Nikola's support troop is
out of the castle.

1256
01:55:27,800 --> 01:55:29,300
Good.

1257
01:55:30,650 --> 01:55:32,020
Good.

1258
01:55:33,650 --> 01:55:36,150
They trust their number.

1259
01:55:38,400 --> 01:55:40,650
But Konur and Boran...

1260
01:55:41,120 --> 01:55:43,720
...are waiting in ambush to crush them.

1261
01:55:47,270 --> 01:55:50,060
They'll understand who we are...

1262
01:55:50,060 --> 01:55:53,120
...once they are trampled
under our horses.

1263
01:55:54,800 --> 01:55:56,950
Is Nikola on the command?

1264
01:55:56,950 --> 01:56:00,150
No, my Bey.
There's another commander on the command.

1265
01:56:01,520 --> 01:56:03,620
He sends his soldiers to death...

1266
01:56:03,620 --> 01:56:06,070
...and hide in the back.
Ignoble.

1267
01:56:08,370 --> 01:56:10,720
Inshallah he doesn't disappear.

1268
01:56:11,250 --> 01:56:12,850
We need him.

1269
01:56:15,470 --> 01:56:17,870
Our preparations are complete.

1270
01:56:24,750 --> 01:56:27,450
He will first lose his soldiers.

1271
01:56:28,620 --> 01:56:30,200
Then his sword.

1272
01:56:32,100 --> 01:56:34,150
Then his life.

1273
01:56:38,270 --> 01:56:39,720
From now on...

1274
01:56:42,020 --> 01:56:44,670
...nothing can save him from death.

1275
01:56:45,950 --> 01:56:48,170
Nothing.

1276
01:56:56,470 --> 01:56:58,300
Let them come, Konur.

1277
01:56:59,250 --> 01:57:02,620
Let them die under
the glorious horses of Turks.

1278
01:57:03,370 --> 01:57:05,570
We haven't been able to enter inside...

1279
01:57:05,570 --> 01:57:08,120
...but destroying them from outside
is improtant too.

1280
01:57:08,120 --> 01:57:09,050
Yes brother.

1281
01:57:09,250 --> 01:57:11,250
Valiants, get ready!

1282
01:57:11,950 --> 01:57:13,630
Hold tight the reins!

1283
01:57:13,630 --> 01:57:15,300
Hold them tight!

1284
01:57:16,120 --> 01:57:18,070
Swing your sword to toss them!

1285
01:57:22,320 --> 01:57:24,150
Infantries are coming from Inegol.

1286
01:57:28,420 --> 01:57:30,450
Brothers!

1287
01:57:30,450 --> 01:57:32,450
Time has come!

1288
01:57:32,450 --> 01:57:38,170
Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest!

1289
01:57:38,170 --> 01:57:39,420
Now!

1290
01:58:43,870 --> 01:58:45,870
Time has come.

1291
01:58:57,850 --> 01:59:00,120
May our war be blessed.

1292
01:59:00,120 --> 01:59:12,700
Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest!

1293
01:59:19,470 --> 01:59:23,100
Turhan, I got the right.
Left is yours, brother.

1294
01:59:26,500 --> 01:59:32,370
Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest!

1295
01:59:32,370 --> 01:59:34,370
They are approaching!

1296
01:59:34,720 --> 02:00:02,820
Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest!

1297
02:00:16,370 --> 02:00:24,850
- Allah is the greatest!
- Allah is the greatest!

1298
02:00:24,850 --> 02:00:26,570
Shields!

1299
02:00:26,570 --> 02:00:30,020
- Allah is the greatest!
- Allah is the greatest!

1300
02:00:35,060 --> 02:00:36,380
Open!

1301
02:00:48,610 --> 02:00:51,610
The end of the road, Osman

1302
02:00:53,320 --> 02:00:56,100
You will pay the price

1303
02:00:56,940 --> 02:00:59,750
And then you will die

1304
02:01:00,670 --> 02:01:03,620
You will die.

1305
02:01:04,110 --> 02:01:05,900
I will grow up.

1306
02:01:13,120 --> 02:01:15,610
They are coming, sir

1307
02:01:16,180 --> 02:01:18,470
What are you talking about, soldier?

1308
02:01:18,640 --> 02:01:21,130
Turks, Turks are coming, sir.

1309
02:01:21,290 --> 02:01:23,720
Turks are at the gates!

1310
02:01:26,210 --> 02:01:28,020
How can this happen?

1311
02:01:33,840 --> 02:01:42,310
Damn, is that impossible?
How can it happen?

1312
02:01:43,120 --> 02:01:51,400
Allah is the greatest!

1313
02:01:59,700 --> 02:02:03,460
Allah is the greatest!

1314
02:02:08,250 --> 02:02:11,710
Allah is the greatest!

1315
02:02:13,630 --> 02:02:15,200
Allah is the greatest!

1316
02:02:22,490 --> 02:02:24,320
Amen.

1317
02:02:25,050 --> 02:02:27,700
In the name of of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

1318
02:02:27,970 --> 02:02:34,090
O our great Allah, make Your
Messenger, his companions,

1319
02:02:34,090 --> 02:02:38,460
and all the saints and
martyrs a support for our army

1320
